  "enhanced_information": "The patient presents with symptoms and ECG findings consistent with an inferior ST-elevation myocardial infarction (STEMI). In such cases, reperfusion pharmacotherapy is critical, and thrombolytics are commonly used. The primary mechanism of action of thrombolytics is the conversion of plasminogen to plasmin, which leads to the breakdown of fibrin in blood clots, restoring blood flow to the affected myocardial tissue. This aligns with the consensus that thrombolytics are essential in treating acute myocardial infarction by dissolving thrombi. Evidence paths confirming the role of plasminogen in myocardial infarction and the action of thrombolytics support this conclusion."
